gy.\n\nReason: Playing at K5 creates a diagonal 4-in-a-row (H8-I7-J6-K5). Even though it is blocked at one end (G9), the other end (L4) is open. This forces the opponent to defend immediately at L4, giving Black the initiative.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "K", "row": 5}'}
